KNOWNBUG (real libstdc++ <tuple>).  std::make_tuple at arity >= 3 returns a
nondeterministic tuple, so std::get reads garbage.  Arity boundary confirmed
(2026-07-14): every arity <= 2 form passes (libstdc++ has a tuple<T1,T2>
partial specialization); every arity >= 3 make_tuple fails.  Direct
construction `std::tuple<int,double,char> t(1,2.0,'a')` WORKS; only
make_tuple's body is lost (its conversion failure is swallowed as a
system-header body, leaving a nondet return).

ROOT (layered, 2026-07-14): converting make_tuple's body fails with
"found no match for symbol '__result_type'".

LAYER 1 (FIXED): the constrained-constructor SFINAE calls folded with an
EMPTY explicit argument list --
_TupleConstraints<1,...>::__is_implicitly_constructible<>() -- because the
constraint alias's own pack `_Args...` was collapsed against stale same-named
zero-size entries in the flat template map; fixed by gating the empty-pack
fallback on deferred_own_pack_names ([temp.alias]/2, [temp.inst]/2).  The
constraints now fold with the full argument list (probe-verified), though for
tuple the verdict happens to be unchanged (an empty __and_<> is vacuously
true).

LAYER 2 (REMAINING): constructor overload resolution for
`__result_type(std::forward<_Elements>(__args)...)` still finds no viable
candidate: the forwarding constructor appears with an unexpanded `? &&`
parameter (its _UElements pack not expanded to three parameters) and the
`const _Elements&...` constructor appears const-STRIPPED (`__decay_t<T> &`),
so nothing binds three forwarded rvalues.  Flip to CORE once the member
constructor-template parameter packs of a class-template instance are
expanded correctly at arity >= 3.
